## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
App links must open correctly from every view. The mode is defined by the **route**, not by screen width:
- **Desktop mode** → URL ends with `.../desktop` (route name `codx-junior-split`). Dockview is mounted, so **multiple** apps can be open simultaneously as panels.
- **Single mode** → **every other route** (chats, kanban, wiki, mobile…). **One** app at a time, addressed only by its route path.

**Root Cause**
`openApp()` currently branches on `$storex.ui.isMobile` (a width check). On a wide screen sitting on a normal route (e.g. `/{project}/chats`), `isMobile` is `false`, so the code tries to create a dockview panel while no dockview is mounted → the link silently does nothing. The correct discriminator is the route: only `.../desktop` supports panels.

**Strategic Approach**
1. Add a single `isDesktopMode()` helper in `navigate.js` derived from `$router.currentRoute.value.name === 'codx-junior-split'`.
2. Replace the `$storex.ui.isMobile` branch in `openApp()` with `!isDesktopMode()` → push route; else → open panel.
3. Make the `$navigation.isDesktopMode` getter delegate to that helper so there is one source of truth (no duplicated string check).

**Dependencies & Risks**
- All callers (`ui.openApp`, `ui.showApp` routing, `apps.openKanban/openMessenger/openWiki/…`, `chats.open`, `meets.open`) funnel through `openApp`, so they all inherit the new behavior — no per-app changes needed.
- `onRouteChanged`'s responsive mobile redirect (`/:projectName/mobile`) and `ui.showApp`'s `!state.isMobile` guard are unrelated to this fix and stay untouched.
- Follow-up (not applied): the header comment in `src/config/apps.js` still says "mobile ROUTE"; it now means "Single mode route".

**Target Files**
- Modify `src/router/navigate.js`

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

`src/router/navigate.js` only, three localized edits:
1. New `MODE DETECTION` section + `isDesktopMode()` helper (before the unified opener).
2. `openApp()` header comment + the mode branch (`!isDesktopMode()` instead of `$storex.ui.isMobile`).
3. `$navigation.isDesktopMode` getter delegates to the helper.

Everything else — route builders, getters, guards, chat/meet/workspace/browser navigation — is unchanged.

## 3. File changes

